address-benchmark is an original implementation, specification and authored
conformance suite. No source code, model, raw address corpus or private listing
extract was copied from the address-normalizer workspace or external projects.

Research cites upstream projects for evaluation concepts, interfaces, provenance
and licensing observations. Those observations are not redistribution grants.
The MIT license here applies to this project's original material only.

Optional installed tools and adapters retain their licenses, including pyperf
(MIT), usaddress (MIT) and its transitive dependencies. Review dependency/model/
corpus notices before packaging or publishing them. No third-party artifacts
are included merely because an optional extra names a package.

The strict-streetline/v1 scoring profile folds values with USPS Publication 28
tables (src/address_benchmark/pub28.py). Pub 28 is a U.S. Government work. The
tables also keep the `observed` non-Pub 28 spellings recorded in the Doorplate
project's Pub 28 data files (https://github.com/jeremeybingham/doorplate,
MIT OR Apache-2.0); those spellings are used here under the MIT license.
